The city of Bordeaux will add 500 electric bicycles to its bike-sharing program next spring, the mayor's office announced on Monday. The new bikes {{1}} at 40 stations, most of them near tram stops and university campuses.

Since its launch three years ago, the program has been {{2}} popular with commuters. Last year, users made more than two million trips. {{3}}

Subscribers will be able to use the electric bikes at no extra cost during the first month. After that, a fee of 50 cents per ride will apply. City officials expect the new bikes to reduce car traffic {{4}} the city center.
